{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPrivate aliases remain across plan-review orchestrator sizing/context/move registries, runner Anthropic/tool/structured-run names, workflow gate-dispatch recovery names, and `llm.config` gate-context names. `llm.usage_log.failure_usage` also misnames the neutral `run_shape` record and has live callers. The governing private-shim policy is the direct prerequisite ADR `earthen-wheat-chick`; the parent container is ordered after the LLM configuration-reader extraction.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the prerequisite ADR and configuration-reader extraction complete, migrate every consumer to `plan_review.sizing`, `context_assembly`, `passes`, `anthropic_model`, `runner_support`, `structured_run`, `workflow.plan_review_recovery`, and `llm.gate_context`. Rename `failure_usage` completely to `run_shape` and prove emitted dictionaries and durable JSONL rows are byte/field identical. Remove each old private binding only after semantic and raw dynamic/monkeypatch census is empty.\n\n## Scope\n\n- plan-review, runner, workflow-dispatch, and gate-context private re-exports\n- usage-log implementation, callers, docs, experiment prose, and JSONL tests\n- all source/test/string/dynamic/monkeypatch consumers\n\n## Testing\n\nRun focused plan-review/workflow/runner suites; compare old/new usage record dictionaries and JSONL rows across success and failure paths; run semantic and raw reference scans.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every enumerated old LLM/workflow private binding has no repository consumer and its named canonical owner is the sole binding.\n- [x] `failure_usage` is absent and `run_shape` owns all former behavior.\n- [x] Success and failure records retain byte/field-identical dictionaries and durable JSONL rows after the rename.\n- [x] Gate-context, plan-review recovery, runner, and workflow behavior remain covered by focused tests.\n- [x] Static, string, dynamic-import, `getattr`, and monkeypatch census proves old paths absent."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788564061149619001,"uuid":"c5716521-53fa-4bbe-b9dd-284ad1e6b44c"}